data: {"seq":44,"turn_id":"task_3dffa8d8fd6cd80f673895cd45cdd59b","type":"turn_result","ts":"2026-11-26T18:25:37.714557+08:00","data":{"outputs":[],"summary":"The tests have passed successfully, indicating that the `moving_averages` function is now working as expected. The function correctly computes the arithmetic mean of every contiguous complete window, including the final one, and returns an empty list if there are no complete windows.\n\nHere's a summary of the changes made:\n1. Modified the `moving_averages` function in `records.py` to handle the final complete window and return an empty list when there are no complete windows.\n2. Added an `__init__.py` file to the `repo` directory to make it importable.\n3. Created a test file `test_moving_averages.py` with test cases to verify the functionality of the `moving_averages` function.\n\nThe function now correctly handles the specified requirements, and the tests confirm its correctness."},"internal":{"source":"worker","type":"result","attempt_id":"9dc85473912d8cafd78025fd32a6de43","task_seq":43,"payload":{"v":1,"ts":"2026-11-26T10:25:37.712Z","seq":33,"type":"result","outputs":[],"summary":"The tests have passed successfully, indicating that the `moving_averages` function is now working as expected. The function correctly computes the arithmetic mean of every contiguous complete window, including the final one, and returns an empty list if there are no complete windows.\n\nHere's a summary of the changes made:\n1. Modified the `moving_averages` function in `records.py` to handle the final complete window and return an empty list when there are no complete windows.\n2. Added an `__init__.py` file to the `repo` directory to make it importable.\n3. Created a test file `test_moving_averages.py` with test cases to verify the functionality of the `moving_averages` function.\n\nThe function now correctly handles the specified requirements, and the tests confirm its correctness.","attempt_id":"9dc85473912d8cafd78025fd32a6de43","session_state":{"state":{"turns":[{"user":"# Rolling averages omit the final complete window\n\nFix `moving_averages` in `records.py`. For positive `width`, return the\narithmetic mean of every contiguous complete window, including the final one.\nReturn an empty list if the input has no complete window.\n\nThe contents of repo/ are already staged at the workspace root. The tool path for the target is exactly records.py. Use read_file on records.py first, write your change to records.py, then run a public smoke test with exec_shell.","reply":"The tests have passed successfully, indicating that the `moving_averages` function is now working as expected. The function correctly computes the arithmetic mean of every contiguous complete window, including the final one, and returns an empty list if there are no complete windows.\n\nHere's a summary of the changes made:\n1. Modified the `moving_averages` function in `records.py` to handle the final complete window and return an empty list when there are no complete windows.\n2. Added an `__init__.py` file to the `repo` directory to make it importable.\n3. Created a test file `test_moving_averages.py` with test cases to verify the functionality of the `moving_averages` function.\n\nThe function now correctly handles the specified requirements, and the tests confirm its correctness.","route":"answer","report":null,"task_id":"task_3dffa8d8fd6cd80f673895cd45cdd59b"}],"sources":[],"schema_version":1},"checkpoint_id":"9979f88ebc384a6b9893e58bc6667b05"}}}}

